Input: {"question": "Which country is Martina Schattkowsky a citizen of?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 69, "text": "**German Historian Martina Schattkowsky: A Proud Citizen of Germany**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 71, "end": 256, "text": "Berlin, Germany - In a world where national identity plays a significant role in shaping our understanding of individuals, it's essential to verify the citizenship of prominent figures."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 257, "end": 383, "text": "In this case, we're delighted to confirm that renowned German historian Martina Schattkowsky is, indeed, a citizen of Germany."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 384, "end": 532, "text": "According to multiple credible sources, including her official biography and academic profiles, Martina Schattkowsky was born and raised in Germany."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 533, "end": 674, "text": "Her extensive research and contributions to the field of history have earned her recognition within the German academic community and beyond."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 675, "end": 808, "text": "\"Martina Schattkowsky is a highly respected historian in Germany, known for her in-depth analysis of modern German history,\" said Dr."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 809, "end": 905, "text": "Andreas Röpcke, a fellow historian and colleague of Schattkowsky's at the University of Leipzig."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 906, "end": 1032, "text": "\"Her work has significantly enriched our understanding of Germany's complex past, and we're proud to call her one of our own.\""}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1033, "end": 1170, "text": "A quick glance at Schattkowsky's curriculum vitae reveals a long list of academic achievements and affiliations with German institutions."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1171, "end": 1320, "text": "She has held positions at the University of Leipzig, the University of Halle-Wittenberg, and the German Historical Institute in Warsaw, among others."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1321, "end": 1400, "text": "These affiliations demonstrate her deep roots in the German academic community."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1401, "end": 1585, "text": "Data from the German Federal Statistical Office (Deutsche Bundesamt für Statistik) shows that Schattkowsky's birthplace and current residence are both located within Germany's borders."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1586, "end": 1706, "text": "This information, combined with her professional affiliations and research focus, leaves no doubt about her citizenship."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1707, "end": 1821, "text": "When asked about her connection to Germany, Schattkowsky herself stated, \"I'm deeply proud to be a German citizen."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1822, "end": 2027, "text": "My country's rich history and cultural heritage have always fascinated me, and I feel fortunate to be able to contribute to the ongoing discussion about our nation's past and its relevance to our present.\""}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2028, "end": 2140, "text": "In conclusion, the evidence overwhelmingly supports the claim that Martina Schattkowsky is a citizen of Germany."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2141, "end": 2274, "text": "Her academic achievements, professional affiliations, and personal statements all point to a strong connection to her native country."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 20, "text": "Martina Schattkowsky"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 22, "end": 152, "text": "Martina Schattkowsky is a German historian, best known for her groundbreaking research on the cultural heritage of Central Europe."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 153, "end": 298, "text": "Despite her German roots, Schattkowsky holds Slovenian citizenship, a fact that has sparked interest among scholars and the general public alike."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 299, "end": 323, "text": "Early Life and Education"}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 325, "end": 393, "text": "Schattkowsky was born on February 12, 1965, in Munich, West Germany."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 394, "end": 518, "text": "She developed an interest in history at a young age, inspired by her parents' stories about their travels to Eastern Europe."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 519, "end": 628, "text": "She pursued her passion at the University of Munich, where she earned a degree in History and Slavic Studies."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 629, "end": 644, "text": "Academic Career"}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 646, "end": 802, "text": "Schattkowsky's academic career took off in the 1990s, when she began researching the cultural exchange between Germany and Slovenia during the Habsburg era."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 803, "end": 921, "text": "Her dissertation, \"The Slovenian Influence on Bavarian Folklore,\" was published in 1995 and received critical acclaim."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 922, "end": 1085, "text": "In 2001, Schattkowsky was appointed as a visiting professor at the University of Ljubljana, where she taught courses on European history and cultural anthropology."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1086, "end": 1230, "text": "During her tenure, she developed close ties with the Slovenian academic community and became an advocate for Slovenian-German cultural exchange."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1231, "end": 1252, "text": "Slovenian Citizenship"}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1254, "end": 1424, "text": "Schattkowsky's connection to Slovenia deepened in 2005, when she was granted Slovenian citizenship in recognition of her contributions to the country's cultural heritage."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1425, "end": 1631, "text": "This decision was met with widespread approval from the Slovenian government and public, who saw it as a symbol of the country's commitment to fostering international cooperation and cultural understanding."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1632, "end": 1654, "text": "Studies and References"}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1656, "end": 1762, "text": "Several studies have explored Schattkowsky's work and its impact on the field of Central European history."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1763, "end": 1991, "text": "A 2010 study published in the Journal of Slavic Studies found that Schattkowsky's research had \"significantly contributed to a greater understanding of the cultural dynamics between Germany and Slovenia during the 19th century.\""}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1992, "end": 1995, "text": "[1]"}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1997, "end": 2197, "text": "In 2015, the Slovenian Ministry of Culture published a comprehensive review of Schattkowsky's work, highlighting her \"tireless efforts to promote Slovenian culture and heritage in Germany and beyond.\""}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2198, "end": 2201, "text": "[2]"}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2203, "end": 2213, "text": "References"}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2215, "end": 2373, "text": "[1] \"The Cultural Exchange between Germany and Slovenia during the 19th Century: A Review of Martina Schattkowsky's Research,\" Journal of Slavic Studies, Vol."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2374, "end": 2381, "text": "23, No."}}, "original_cards": [], "current_answers": ["Germany", "Slovenia"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Germany", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Slovenia", "origin": "initial"}]}
